  "body": "## What changed\n\nNative AI chat waits for Allow/Deny before it runs any `delete_*` tool.\nEach delete call uses the existing confirmation banner.\nDeny leaves the document unchanged and returns a refusal to the model.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe native confirmation guard covered project opening and the live approval rules.\nThose rules did not include document deletes.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `native_confirmation_covers_every_published_delete_tool` covers all published delete tools and preserves ordinary read and add behavior.\n- `native_two_deletes_wait_for_confirmation_and_denial_preserves_job` denies two local Native calls and compares the full job and history.\n  It checks both refusal messages and then approves both deletes in a new turn.\n- Both tests failed before the fix and passed after the fix.\n- Mutation: restore the upstream guard with the tests retained; both tests fail.\n  Restore the fix; both tests pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 10 steps passed, no failures.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- The heavy plan reaches no lanes.\n- The inherited sccache build stalled.\n  Checks passed with the wrapper disabled and a separate build directory inside the worktree.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nLive model endpoints and manual desktop interaction were not exercised.\nOther delete tools have policy coverage; the scripted document test uses `delete_operation`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found for the changed files.\n\nChangelog: AI chat now requires Allow/Deny before native delete tools change the document.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3424\n\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThese captures use the shipping AI Chat panel and a scripted local Native transport.\nThe fixture requests deletion of two Face operations through the normal worker and MCP commands.\n\nBefore: the original confirmation guard runs both deletes and shows their successful results.\n\n![Native delete results before the fix](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/pr-3438/before.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter: the fixed guard keeps both operations and waits for Allow or Deny before the first delete.\n\n![Allow/Deny confirmation after the fix](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/pr-3438/after.png?raw=true)\n",
